+# Review Diff File Workflow
+
+Status: current review-diff-file workflow  
+Doc version: v0.1.0  
+Scope: default post-apply review transfer for replacement archives; repo-stored diff artifact workflow
+
+## 1. Purpose
+
+This workflow owns the default archive review transfer mode.
+
+When the assistant gives a replacement archive/package, the user should not have to paste a large diff into chat. The default archive apply commands should create review diff files inside the repository, and the assistant should later read those files from the target repo/branch/path.
+
+## 2. Default Mode
+
+Default archive review mode:
+
+```text
+review-diff-file mode
+```
+
+Standard files:
+
+```text
+_ai-review-diffs/last-archive.diff
+_ai-review-diffs/last-archive-summary.md
+```
+
+Meaning:
+
+```text
+- `_ai-review-diffs/last-archive.diff` contains the scoped diff of the applied archive changes.
+- `_ai-review-diffs/last-archive-summary.md` identifies repo, branch, mode, changed files and the chat review command.
+- These files are review artifacts.
+- The actual archive replacement files remain local and uncommitted until review is complete.
+```
+
+## 3. Command Families
+
+Archive creation commands use this mode by default:
+
+```text
+давай архив
+собери архив
+replacement package
+archive for manual apply
+```
+
+Explicit aliases for the same default mode:
+
+```text
+давай архив с дифф-файлом
+давай архив с review diff file
+архив с дифф-файлом
+архив без вставки диффа
+review-diff archive
+```
+
+Review command:
+
+```text
+проверь review diff file
+проверь diff file
+review diff file
+```
+
+## 4. Required Assistant Response Shape
+
+When the assistant provides an archive, the final response should include:
+
+```text
+1. Archive link.
+2. Apply command.
+3. Separate command to commit and push only review diff files.
+4. Short instruction telling the user what to say after pushing the review diff file.
+5. `План файл-обновление` when applicable.
+```
+
+The apply command creates the review diff files but does not commit them.
+
+The separate commit/push command stages, commits and pushes only:
+
+```text
+_ai-review-diffs/last-archive.diff
+_ai-review-diffs/last-archive-summary.md
+```
+
+## 5. Hard Boundary
+
+Allowed before diff review:
+
+```text
+- commit and push `_ai-review-diffs/last-archive.diff`;
+- commit and push `_ai-review-diffs/last-archive-summary.md`.
+```
+
+Forbidden before diff review:
+
+```text
+- commit real archive replacement files;
+- push real archive replacement files;
+- use `git add .`;
+- stage files outside the review diff artifact list in the review-diff commit.
+```
+
+The review-diff commit is not approval of the real archive changes. It only makes the diff readable from the repository.
+
+## 6. Apply Command Requirements
+
+The archive apply command must:
+
+```text
+1. pull the target branch;
+2. apply replacement files to the local repo;
+3. define `$files` for all real files changed by the archive;
+4. define `$newFiles` for expected new real files;
+5. make expected new files visible in the diff with `git add -N`;
+6. generate `_ai-review-diffs/last-archive.diff`;
+7. generate `_ai-review-diffs/last-archive-summary.md`;
+8. unstage real files after diff generation;
+9. print the review paths and the no-real-commit warning.
+```
+
+It must not:
+
+```text
+- commit real files;
+- push real files;
+- copy the full diff to clipboard by default;
+- ask the user to paste a giant diff into chat by default.
+```
+
+## 7. Review-Diff-Only Commit Command Requirements
+
+The assistant response must include a separate PowerShell block that:
+
+```text
+1. unstages everything;
+2. stages only the two review diff files;
+3. checks that no other file is staged;
+4. runs `git diff --cached --check`;
+5. commits with a review-diff-only message;
+6. pushes the target branch.
+```
+
+Required staged-file guard:
+
+```text
+foreach ($f in $staged) {
+  if ($reviewFiles -notcontains $f) {
+    throw "Unexpected staged file. Refusing review-diff commit: $f"
+  }
+}
+```
+
+## 8. Chat Review Command
+
+After the review diff files are pushed, the user can tell the chat:
+
+```text
+проверь review diff file
+
+Repo: <owner/repo>
+Branch: <branch>
+Path: _ai-review-diffs/last-archive.diff
+```
+
+If the active repo/branch/path are already clear from the current archive context, the user may say only:
+
+```text
+проверь review diff file
+```
+
+If repo, branch or path are unclear, the chat should ask for the missing value. It should not ask the user to paste the full diff unless repo access is unavailable.
+
+## 9. Review Behavior
+
+When reviewing the diff file, the chat should check:
+
+```text
+- only intended real files appear in the diff;
+- all expected new real files appear;
+- no unrelated files or sections are modified;
+- package intent matches the diff;
+- review artifact files are not confused with real archive changes;
+- final real commit commands, if given after approval, stage only intended real files.
+```
+
+If the diff is OK, then and only then the assistant may provide the real commit/push command for the actual archive files.
+
+## 10. Fallback
+
+Clipboard diff transfer is a fallback only when repo-stored review diff is not possible.
+
+Examples:
+
+```text
+- no repo/branch access;
+- user explicitly asks for clipboard/pasted diff;
+- target repo policy forbids committing review artifacts.
+```
+
+In fallback mode, keep the old clipboard-safe rules: save diff to a file, read it with UTF-8, then copy to clipboard. Do not print the full diff to terminal.
